# Any authentication event, failed OR successful, reaching a login service
# from outside your home countries. Thirteen banishing rules, one per daemon, each
# carrying its service's whole offense vocabulary plus the successful login on
# top, gated on country_codes{home} and scored so that ONE event is enough.
# For the drive-by that probes a handful of credentials and moves on, which no
# per-service threshold is fast enough to catch. Reference as
# %syslog/foreign-auth%.
#
# THREE THINGS BEFORE YOU LIST THIS.
#
# 1. It does nothing until you define country_codes{home} in the config, and
#    it refuses to load, loudly, if you list it without them. It also needs
#    geoip_db and IP::Geolocation::MMDB. The gate fails closed, so an address
#    the database cannot place is not banished... internal addresses included,
#    which never locate.
#
# 2. ORDER. List this group AHEAD of the per-service rules it shadows
#    (syslog/sshd, syslog/dovecot, syslog/postfix-sasl, and the rest). A rule
#    whose country gate vetoes does not consume the line, so a domestic event
#    falls straight through and is counted by the ordinary rule exactly as
#    before. Listed after them, the ordinary rules consume the failures first
#    and only foreign successes reach these.
#
# 3. It banishes on a SUCCESSFUL login. That is the point... a right password
#    from a country you do no business with is worse news than a wrong one...
#    but it means an admin logging in from abroad is banished mid-session by
#    their own good credentials. Set eve_only and watch it for a week before
#    letting it act. openvpn especially: a VPN reached from abroad is usually
#    the entire reason the VPN exists.
#
# The three %syslog/...-foreign-login% rules are the gentler policy for the
# same ground: they sight a foreign SUCCESS and banish nobody. Run one family
# or the other per service, not both... whichever is listed first consumes the
# successes and the other never sees them.
#
# See docs/rules.md (Rule groups, and the country gate).

syslog/courier-foreign-auth
syslog/cyrus-imap-foreign-auth
syslog/dovecot-foreign-auth
syslog/dropbear-foreign-auth
syslog/openvpn-foreign-auth
syslog/perdition-foreign-auth
syslog/postfix-sasl-foreign-auth
syslog/proftpd-foreign-auth
syslog/pure-ftpd-foreign-auth
syslog/sshd-foreign-auth
syslog/uwimap-foreign-auth
syslog/vsftpd-foreign-auth
syslog/wuftpd-foreign-auth
